# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream repository -- deliberately NOT vendored.
#
# The central claim of this repo is that the authors' own functions were called
# unmodified. A reader who clones upstream at the pinned commit themselves gets
# stronger evidence than a vendored copy they would have to diff. ./setup.sh
# clones it to exactly this path, which experiments/compat.py hardcodes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ai-economist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-shippable material.
#
# These patterns are a second line of defence only. The actual exclusion is
# physical: the private material lives outside this repo, in
# ../_private_ai-economist-talk/ . Relying on ignore patterns alone would make
# the pre-push leak gate pass vacuously -- `git status` cannot see an ignored
# file, so a stale PDF still sitting in the tree would look identical to a clean
# tree. The gate therefore uses `find`, not `git status`, for these types.
#
#   *.pdf   paywalled papers (Saez 2001 is Oxford Academic subscription content)
#   *.csv   KakaoTalk group-chat export naming five third parties
#   *.m4a   NotebookLM-generated derivative audio
#   *.mhtml saved copyrighted web pages
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pdf
*.csv
*.m4a
*.mhtml

# Python environment / caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Agent + editor session state (local transcripts and logs)
.remember/
.omc/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# macOS
.DS_Store
__MACOSX/
